---
layout: changelog
title: Announcing Appwrite 2.2 for self-hosted deployments
date: 2026-09-15
cover: /images/changelog/2026-09-15.avif
tags: auth, messaging, functions, console, infrastructure
---

Appwrite 2.2 is now available for self-hosting.

This release includes:

- [Email policies](/docs/products/auth/email-policies) on self-hosted instances. Block sign-ups from disposable, free, corporate, or aliased email addresses from the Auth policies page in the Console or through the project API
- Alphanumeric sender IDs for Twilio. The `from` field on the Twilio provider and `_APP_SMS_FROM` accept a sender name as well as a phone number
- Function and site executions stored in ClickHouse only. The `_APP_EXECUTIONS_DUAL_WRITE` variable is removed
- A batch of fixes to Appwrite Console, including manual deployments from `.tar.gz` files on macOS and activity and realtime pages that work on mobile

Head over to our [migration guide](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production/updates#upgrading-to-2-2) to upgrade your instance. Upgrade to 2.1.0 first if you are still on 2.0.0.

For the complete list of updates and fixes, check out the [release notes](https://github.com/appwrite/appwrite/releases/tag/2.2.0) on GitHub.

